WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:19.000
Cheedeb presents, Zorro, by Johnston McCully.

00:31.000 --> 00:38.950
This story takes place in Spanish, California during the first part of the 1800s.

00:39.000 --> 00:43.950
The word Zorro means Fox in Spanish.

00:44.000 --> 00:51.000
The story of Zorro is an old legend from Spanish, California.

00:52.000 --> 00:56.950
Chapter 1. A Stormy Night

00:57.000 --> 01:02.950
Reina de Los Angeles is a Spanish village in Southern California.

01:03.000 --> 01:09.950
In the village, there is a military procedure with Spanish soldiers and their horses.

01:10.000 --> 01:14.950
There is also a Spanish church called a mission.

01:15.000 --> 01:17.950
The Spanish friars live here.

01:18.000 --> 01:25.950
All around the village, there are big homes with patios.

01:26.000 --> 01:35.950
Tonight, there is a terrible storm, and it is raining.

01:36.000 --> 01:40.950
Inside the village tavern, there are soldiers and other men.

01:41.000 --> 01:44.950
They are eating and drinking.

01:45.000 --> 01:48.950
Sergeant Pedro Gonzalez is at the tavern.

01:49.000 --> 01:52.950
He is a big, strong man.

01:53.000 --> 01:54.950
What a horrible night.

01:55.000 --> 01:57.950
It always rains in February.

01:58.000 --> 02:02.950
Where is Zorro on this stormy night? Asks one soldier.

02:03.000 --> 02:05.950
Zorro, don't say that name.

02:06.000 --> 02:11.950
He is abandoned and a criminal. Says Sergeant Gonzalez.

02:12.000 --> 02:16.950
He is the terror of Southern California. Says another soldier.

02:17.000 --> 02:20.950
People say that he takes from the rich and gives to the poor.

02:21.000 --> 02:24.950
He is a friend of the natives and the friars.

02:25.000 --> 02:28.950
He punishes dishonest people, says an old man.

02:29.000 --> 02:32.950
Huh, Zorro is a big mystery.

02:33.000 --> 02:35.950
Who is he? Where is he from?

02:36.000 --> 02:39.950
He wears a black mask and no one can see his face.

02:40.000 --> 02:44.950
He travels on the El Camino Real on his fast horse.

02:45.000 --> 02:48.950
He is very good with his sword. Says the Sergeant.

02:49.000 --> 02:51.950
Yes, and he leaves his mark.

02:52.000 --> 02:56.950
The Z, everywhere. Says the old man.

02:57.000 --> 02:58.950
No one can stop him.

02:59.000 --> 03:03.950
The governor of California offers a big reward for the capture of Zorro.

03:04.000 --> 03:07.950
Says one soldier.

03:08.000 --> 03:10.950
At that moment, a man enters the tavern.

03:11.000 --> 03:12.950
He is young and handsome.

03:13.000 --> 03:15.950
He has black hair and dark eyes.

03:16.000 --> 03:17.950
He has fine clothes.

03:18.000 --> 03:23.950
Don Diego Vega, my friend. Says Sergeant Gonzalez.

03:24.000 --> 03:25.950
Your clothes are wet.

03:26.000 --> 03:29.950
Why are you out on this rainy night?

03:30.000 --> 03:31.950
Don Diego smiles and says,

03:32.000 --> 03:35.950
I am going home, but I am cold and wet.

03:36.000 --> 03:38.950
I want something to drink.

03:39.000 --> 03:41.950
Come and stand near the fire. Says the Sergeant.

03:42.000 --> 03:44.950
Here is a glass of wine.

03:45.000 --> 03:47.950
Thank you, my friend. Says Don Diego.

03:48.000 --> 03:49.950
We are talking about Zorro.

03:50.000 --> 03:53.950
Everyone is scared of him, but I am not.

03:54.000 --> 03:56.950
I am ready to fight Zorro and win.

03:57.000 --> 03:58.950
I am a champion with the sword.

03:59.000 --> 04:02.950
What do you think, Don Diego? Ask the Sergeant.

04:03.000 --> 04:06.950
Everyone talks about this mysterious man with a mask.

04:07.000 --> 04:10.950
Many people say good things about him. Says Don Diego.

04:11.000 --> 04:13.950
I want to fight him and capture him.

04:14.000 --> 04:17.950
I want the big reward. Says Sergeant Gonzalez.

04:18.000 --> 04:18.950
No, no.

04:19.000 --> 04:20.950
Don't talk about fighting.

04:21.000 --> 04:22.950
I hate fighting and I hate violence.

04:23.000 --> 04:24.950
I think Zorro is sincere.

04:25.000 --> 04:27.950
He punishes only bad people.

04:28.000 --> 04:31.950
He protects the poor, the natives and the friars.

04:32.000 --> 04:35.950
Let Zorro do his work. Says Don Diego.

04:36.000 --> 04:37.950
You are a kind man.

04:38.000 --> 04:39.950
You like music and poetry.

04:40.000 --> 04:42.950
You don't understand, my friend.

04:43.000 --> 04:46.950
You are rich and noble. Says the Sergeant.

04:47.000 --> 04:48.950
Don Diego smiles and says,

04:49.000 --> 04:51.950
It's 6 p.m. I must return to my hacienda.

04:52.000 --> 04:53.950
Good night, everyone.

04:54.000 --> 04:59.000
He opens the tavern door and goes out into the rain.

05:03.000 --> 05:07.950
Chapter 2, a surprise visit.

05:08.000 --> 05:12.950
At 7 p.m. the door of the tavern opens.

05:13.000 --> 05:18.950
Sergeant Gonzalez and the other soldiers are standing near the fire.

05:19.000 --> 05:24.950
They are talking about Don Diego Vega and his rich family.

05:25.000 --> 05:28.950
They turn around and see a man.

05:29.000 --> 05:31.950
He is dressed in black.

05:32.000 --> 05:35.950
He has a black mask and a black sombrero.

05:36.000 --> 05:37.950
It is Zorro.

05:38.000 --> 05:40.950
Good evening. My name is Zorro.

05:41.000 --> 05:42.950
Says the masked man.

05:43.000 --> 05:47.950
The men in the tavern are very surprised and scared.

05:48.000 --> 05:51.950
Sergeant Gonzalez looks at him carefully and says,

05:52.000 --> 05:55.000
What do you want, Bandit?

05:56.000 --> 05:57.950
Zorro laughs loudly.

05:58.000 --> 06:00.950
He looks at Sergeant Gonzalez and says,

06:01.000 --> 06:03.950
I am here to punish you, Sergeant.

06:04.000 --> 06:07.950
What do you mean? Says the Sergeant.

06:08.000 --> 06:09.950
You beat the poor natives.

06:10.000 --> 06:11.950
I'm a friend of the natives.

06:12.000 --> 06:15.950
I am here to punish you. You idiot.

06:16.000 --> 06:19.950
The governor wants you dead or alive. Says Sergeant Gonzalez.

06:20.000 --> 06:23.950
He pulls out his sword and wants to fight.

06:24.000 --> 06:27.950
At that moment, Zorro pulls out a pistol.

06:28.000 --> 06:30.950
He watches everyone carefully.

06:31.000 --> 06:34.950
Sergeant Gonzalez looks at the pistol and says,

06:35.000 --> 06:37.950
Courageous men don't use pistols.

06:38.000 --> 06:39.950
They use swords.

06:40.000 --> 06:42.950
Perhaps you are not courageous, Zorro.

06:43.000 --> 06:46.950
This pistol is necessary because you have many friends in this tavern.

06:47.000 --> 06:51.000
Everyone must go near the fire and stay there. Says Zorro.

06:52.000 --> 06:54.950
Now I have a pistol in my left hand and a sword in my right hand.

06:55.000 --> 06:56.950
I am ready to punish you.

06:57.000 --> 07:00.000
Fight, Senor! Says the Sergeant.

07:01.000 --> 07:02.950
They start fighting.

07:03.000 --> 07:06.950
Their swords move quickly and make a lot of noise.

07:07.000 --> 07:09.950
The two men are good fighters.

07:10.000 --> 07:12.950
Zorro is fast and light.

07:13.000 --> 07:15.950
Sergeant Gonzalez is slow and heavy.

07:16.000 --> 07:18.950
Zorro jumps onto a table.

07:19.000 --> 07:20.950
Then he jumps onto a chair.

07:21.000 --> 07:26.950
The fight continues and Sergeant Gonzalez's sword falls onto the floor.

07:27.000 --> 07:28.950
His face is white.

07:29.000 --> 07:30.950
He is scared.

07:31.000 --> 07:33.950
Zorro slaps his face and says,

07:34.000 --> 07:36.950
This is your punishment.

07:37.000 --> 07:42.950
Then he makes a Z on the Sergeant's shirt with his sword.

07:43.000 --> 07:44.950
Zorro runs to the window.

07:45.000 --> 07:47.950
He opens it and says,

07:48.000 --> 07:49.950
Good evening, gentlemen.

07:50.000 --> 07:54.000
He jumps out of the window and disappears.

07:57.000 --> 07:58.950
Chapter 3.

07:59.000 --> 08:02.000
The Pulido Hacienda

08:03.000 --> 08:05.950
The next day is warm and sunny.

08:06.000 --> 08:09.950
Don Diego gets on his beautiful horse.

08:10.000 --> 08:15.000
He rides to Don Carlos Pulido's big Hacienda.

08:16.000 --> 08:19.950
Don Carlos is a good friend of Don Diego's family.

08:20.000 --> 08:23.950
Both families are rich and important.

08:24.000 --> 08:26.950
But the governor does not like Don Carlos.

08:27.000 --> 08:29.950
He creates problems for him.

08:30.000 --> 08:32.950
He wants to take Don Carlos's land.

08:33.000 --> 08:35.950
Don Carlos is happy to see his friend.

08:36.000 --> 08:37.950
Good morning, Don Diego.

08:38.000 --> 08:39.950
What a nice surprise.

08:40.000 --> 08:41.950
Come and sit in the patio.

08:42.000 --> 08:42.950
Thank you.

08:43.000 --> 08:46.950
I am here to say something very important. Says Don Diego.

08:47.000 --> 08:49.950
I am almost 25 years old.

08:50.000 --> 08:52.950
My father wants me to get married and start a family.

08:53.000 --> 08:55.950
I am not interested in marriage.

08:56.000 --> 08:57.950
I think love and marriage are boring.

08:58.000 --> 08:59.950
But I must obey my father.

09:00.000 --> 09:04.950
How old is your daughter Lolita? Asks Don Diego.

09:05.000 --> 09:09.950
Lolita is 18 years old and she is very beautiful. Answers Don Carlos.

09:10.000 --> 09:11.950
You have a fine family.

09:12.000 --> 09:16.950
With your permission, I want to marry your daughter. Says Don Diego.

09:17.000 --> 09:19.950
Don Carlos smiles and is happy.

09:20.000 --> 09:21.950
This is an honor for our family.

09:22.000 --> 09:23.950
You have my permission.

09:24.000 --> 09:25.950
Do you want to see Lolita?

09:26.000 --> 09:29.950
I think I must. Answers Don Diego.

09:30.000 --> 09:33.950
Don Carlos calls her and she comes to the patio.

09:34.000 --> 09:38.950
Lolita is a lovely girl with long black hair and dark eyes.

09:39.000 --> 09:40.950
Good morning, Senorita.

09:41.000 --> 09:44.950
There is something I must tell you. Says Don Diego smiling.

09:45.000 --> 09:47.950
I want to marry you and your father approves.

09:48.000 --> 09:50.950
Oh, Senor. Exclaims Lolita.

09:51.000 --> 09:52.950
You want to marry me?

09:53.000 --> 09:56.950
She is surprised and her face is red.

09:57.000 --> 09:58.950
Think about it today.

09:59.000 --> 10:01.950
One of my servants can bring me your answer tomorrow.

10:02.000 --> 10:05.950
But why can't you come tomorrow? Asks Lolita.

10:06.000 --> 10:08.950
Oh, your hussy end is far.

10:09.000 --> 10:10.950
I get tired when I ride my horse.

10:11.000 --> 10:13.950
I prefer to stay at home and rest.

10:14.000 --> 10:14.950
What?

10:15.000 --> 10:18.950
You want to marry me and you don't want to visit me?

10:19.000 --> 10:21.950
Is this your idea of love?

10:22.000 --> 10:25.950
I want to marry a strong romantic man.

10:26.000 --> 10:30.950
You are young and rich, but you are not strong or romantic.

10:31.000 --> 10:33.950
Do you have a heart? Says Lolita.

10:34.000 --> 10:35.950
She is angry.

10:36.000 --> 10:38.950
She runs away and tells her mother.

10:39.000 --> 10:40.950
Donna Catalina says...

10:41.000 --> 10:42.950
You are lucky Lolita.

10:43.000 --> 10:45.950
Don Diego is very rich.

10:46.000 --> 10:48.950
He comes from a noble family.

10:49.000 --> 10:50.950
The governor likes his family.

10:51.000 --> 10:54.950
This is a big opportunity for our family.

10:55.000 --> 10:58.950
In the afternoon, Lolita is alone in the patio.

10:59.000 --> 11:01.950
She is thinking about Don Diego.

11:02.000 --> 11:05.950
Suddenly, she hears a noise and turns around.

11:06.000 --> 11:08.950
She sees Zorro standing in front of her.

11:09.000 --> 11:09.950
Zorro.

11:10.000 --> 11:10.950
She whispers.

11:11.000 --> 11:12.950
Don't be afraid, Senorita.

11:13.000 --> 11:15.950
I only punish corrupt people.

11:16.000 --> 11:17.950
I like your father because he is honest.

11:18.000 --> 11:19.950
I'm here to admire your beauty.

11:20.000 --> 11:22.950
What? You must go away.

11:23.000 --> 11:26.950
You are in great danger. Says Lolita.

11:27.000 --> 11:30.950
You are beautiful and kind, Lolita. Says Zorro.

11:31.000 --> 11:32.950
You kiss your hand.

11:33.000 --> 11:35.950
Zorro takes her small hand and kisses it.

11:36.000 --> 11:40.950
Lolita looks into his eyes and smiles.

11:41.000 --> 11:42.950
Then she runs into the house.

11:43.000 --> 11:45.950
What a courageous man.

11:46.000 --> 11:48.950
He is a bandit, but I like him.

11:49.000 --> 11:51.000
Lolita thinks.

11:53.000 --> 11:54.950
Spanish California.

11:55.000 --> 12:00.950
Read this page from a Spanish friars diary and learn about Spanish California.

12:01.000 --> 12:03.950
San Diego de Alcala.

12:04.000 --> 12:06.950
April 22, 1802.

12:07.000 --> 12:09.950
California is a beautiful place.

12:10.000 --> 12:12.950
It is always warm and sunny.

12:13.000 --> 12:16.950
There are flowers and fruit trees everywhere.

12:17.000 --> 12:20.950
I live in the San Diego de Alcala mission.

12:21.000 --> 12:22.950
Other friars live here too.

12:23.000 --> 12:26.950
San Diego de Alcala is the first Californian mission.

12:27.000 --> 12:30.950
Many Indians live in the village near the mission.

12:31.000 --> 12:32.950
They are friendly.

12:33.000 --> 12:35.950
We teach them many things.

12:36.000 --> 12:38.950
Spanish families live here too.

12:39.000 --> 12:42.950
Some rich families have big haciendas.

12:43.000 --> 12:47.950
The village of San Diego de Alcala is growing quickly.

12:48.000 --> 12:50.950
It is near the Pacific Ocean.

12:51.000 --> 12:55.950
Spanish ships often come and bring things from Spain.

12:56.000 --> 12:59.950
Some villages have military presidios.

13:00.000 --> 13:03.950
Spanish soldiers live in the presidios.

13:04.000 --> 13:08.950
Today, friar Junipero Serra is visiting us.

13:09.000 --> 13:11.950
He is a very important friar.

13:12.000 --> 13:15.950
He travels and builds missions in California.

13:16.000 --> 13:19.950
He wants to build 21 missions.

13:20.000 --> 13:22.950
Some big missions in California are

13:23.000 --> 13:38.950
San Juan Capistrano, Reina de Los Angeles, Santa Barbara, San Luis Obispo, Carmel, San Francisco.

13:39.000 --> 13:43.950
Chapter 4, Captain Ramon.

13:44.000 --> 13:48.950
At 8 p.m., it is dinner time at Don Carlos's home.

13:49.000 --> 13:51.950
The family is sitting at the table.

13:52.000 --> 13:54.950
Someone knocks at the door.

13:55.000 --> 13:57.950
A servant opens it.

13:58.000 --> 14:00.950
And Zorro appears.

14:01.000 --> 14:04.950
Don Carlos, his wife and daughter, stand up.

14:05.000 --> 14:06.950
They are scared.

14:07.000 --> 14:08.950
Good evening, says Zorro.

14:09.000 --> 14:10.950
Don't be scared.

14:11.000 --> 14:12.950
You are an honest man, Don Carlos.

14:13.000 --> 14:15.950
I only want some food and drink.

14:16.000 --> 14:18.950
Zorro goes to Lolita and whispers.

14:19.000 --> 14:21.950
I cannot forget this afternoon in the patio.

14:22.000 --> 14:23.950
You must not come here.

14:24.000 --> 14:27.950
It is dangerous. Whispers Lolita.

14:28.000 --> 14:31.950
Suddenly, a young Spanish soldier enters the house.

14:32.000 --> 14:33.950
He is Captain Ramon.

14:34.000 --> 14:36.950
He wants to arrest Zorro.

14:37.000 --> 14:39.950
Zorro takes out his sword and they fight.

14:40.000 --> 14:42.950
The two men are good fighters.

14:43.000 --> 14:46.950
I want to arrest you, Zorro! Says Captain Ramon.

14:47.000 --> 14:48.950
You are a public enemy!

14:49.000 --> 14:51.950
You cannot arrest me, says Zorro.

14:52.000 --> 14:57.950
Zorro injures the Captain's shoulder with his sword.

14:58.000 --> 14:59.950
The Captain falls to the floor.

15:00.000 --> 15:01.950
Please help the Captain.

15:02.000 --> 15:12.950
Zorro says to Don Carlos, then he smiles at Lolita and rides away on his horse.

15:13.000 --> 15:18.950
Don Carlos' wife and daughter look after Captain Ramon's injured shoulder.

15:19.000 --> 15:21.950
The Captain likes beautiful Lolita.

15:22.000 --> 15:24.950
Don Carlos, says the Captain.

15:25.000 --> 15:26.950
I like Lolita very much.

15:27.000 --> 15:31.950
I come from a good family and I am the Governor's friend.

15:32.000 --> 15:35.950
I'm 23 years old and I am the Captain of the Presidio.

15:36.000 --> 15:38.950
May I court Lolita.

15:39.000 --> 15:42.950
First, I must explain something. Says Don Carlos.

15:43.000 --> 15:46.950
Don Diego Vega wants to court Lolita too.

15:47.000 --> 15:53.950
Lolita must choose her husband herself, but you have my permission to court her.

15:54.000 --> 15:57.950
The next morning, there is a lot of noise at the Presidio.

15:58.000 --> 16:01.950
Don Diego and other men are watching.

16:02.000 --> 16:04.950
There are many soldiers on their horses.

16:05.000 --> 16:09.950
They are listening to Sergeant Gonzales.

16:10.000 --> 16:12.950
Today is an important day.

16:13.000 --> 16:14.950
We must find Zorro.

16:15.000 --> 16:18.950
We must look in every Hacienda and in every home.

16:19.000 --> 16:21.950
Remember the Governor's big reward.

16:22.000 --> 16:23.950
Let's go!

16:24.000 --> 16:28.950
That morning, Don Diego sends a letter to Don Carlos.

16:29.000 --> 16:33.950
My dear friend, Sergeant Gonzales and his soldiers want to arrest Zorro.

16:34.000 --> 16:37.950
It is dangerous for you and your family to stay at your Hacienda.

16:38.000 --> 16:41.950
Please come to my home in Reina de Los Angeles.

16:42.000 --> 16:43.950
It is safe in my home.

16:44.000 --> 16:45.950
I must go away for a few days.

16:46.000 --> 16:48.950
Your friend, Diego Vega.

16:49.000 --> 16:52.950
Don Carlos receives the letter and says...

16:53.000 --> 16:54.950
What a generous invitation.

16:55.000 --> 16:56.950
Don Diego wants to protect Lolita.

16:57.000 --> 16:59.950
We must accept the invitation.

17:00.000 --> 17:02.000
Let us go immediately.

17:05.000 --> 17:06.950
Chapter 5.

17:07.000 --> 17:09.950
Lolita is in love.

17:10.000 --> 17:14.950
Don Diego's home in Reina de Los Angeles is big and beautiful.

17:15.000 --> 17:18.950
There are many rooms and many servants.

17:19.000 --> 17:22.950
There is a big garden with trees and flowers.

17:23.000 --> 17:25.950
Don Carlos and his family like it.

17:26.000 --> 17:31.950
Lolita, Mary Don Diego and this beautiful home is yours.

17:32.000 --> 17:33.950
She says Dona Catalina.

17:34.000 --> 17:35.950
I don't love Don Diego.

17:36.000 --> 17:38.950
I don't want to marry him. Says Lolita.

17:39.000 --> 17:44.950
Lolita, tonight your mother and I must visit our old friends. Says Don Carlos.

17:45.000 --> 17:46.950
Can you stay at home alone?

17:47.000 --> 17:48.950
Yes, of course.

17:49.000 --> 17:51.950
There are many books in Don Diego's library.

17:52.000 --> 17:54.950
I can stay here and read.

17:55.000 --> 17:56.950
Lolita looks at the books.

17:57.000 --> 17:58.950
How strange.

17:59.000 --> 17:59.950
She thinks.

18:00.000 --> 18:06.950
Don Diego has books about love, passion, adventure, horses and heroes.

18:07.000 --> 18:08.950
But he isn't strong.

18:09.000 --> 18:10.950
It is so lifeless.

18:11.000 --> 18:13.950
Suddenly there is a knock at the door.

18:14.000 --> 18:20.950
A servant opens it and Captain Ramon enters.

18:21.000 --> 18:24.950
He goes to the library and sees Lolita.

18:25.000 --> 18:26.950
I'm glad you are alone.

18:27.000 --> 18:29.950
You are a very beautiful girl.

18:30.000 --> 18:32.950
I have your father's permission to court you.

18:33.000 --> 18:38.950
I know that Don Diego wants to marry you, but I am superior in every way.

18:39.000 --> 18:40.950
Don Diego has no courage.

18:41.000 --> 18:42.950
He is a weak man.

18:43.000 --> 18:45.950
I am the captain of the Presidio.

18:46.000 --> 18:48.950
I am alone. Says Lolita.

18:49.000 --> 18:50.950
You cannot stay here.

18:51.000 --> 18:51.950
It is not right.

18:52.000 --> 18:53.950
Please go away.

18:54.000 --> 18:58.950
Captain Ramon takes her hand and says, don't run away, Lolita.

18:59.000 --> 19:00.950
You are mine.

19:01.000 --> 19:02.950
Kiss me.

19:03.000 --> 19:06.950
Lolita pushes him away and says, I don't want to kiss you.

19:07.000 --> 19:08.950
Go away.

19:09.000 --> 19:10.950
No, you are mine.

19:11.000 --> 19:12.950
You must marry me.

19:13.000 --> 19:15.950
Now kiss me.

19:16.000 --> 19:19.950
Lolita slaps the captain's face.

19:20.000 --> 19:26.950
At that moment, Zorro appears in the library and says, Captain Ramon, you are a villain.

19:27.000 --> 19:28.950
Don't touch Lolita.

19:29.000 --> 19:30.950
Leave this house immediately.

19:31.000 --> 19:36.950
I cannot forget this terrible insult. Says the captain.

19:37.000 --> 19:38.950
His face is red with anger.

19:39.000 --> 19:43.950
Zorro opens the door and kicks him out.

19:44.000 --> 19:46.950
Thank you for your help, Zorro.

19:47.000 --> 19:49.950
You are courageous and kind.

19:50.000 --> 19:51.950
I love you.

19:52.000 --> 19:57.950
Lolita says, Dear Lolita, I love you too, says Zorro.

19:58.000 --> 20:01.000
They embrace and kiss.

20:04.000 --> 20:05.950
Chapter 6.

20:06.000 --> 20:08.950
Friar Felipe.

20:09.000 --> 20:12.950
Captain Ramon returns to the Presidio.

20:13.000 --> 20:14.950
He is furious.

20:15.000 --> 20:20.950
I must punish Lolita, her family and Zorro for their insults.

20:21.000 --> 20:23.950
He thinks, I must write a letter to the governor.

20:24.000 --> 20:29.950
I must tell him that Don Carlos Pulido and his family are traitors.

20:30.000 --> 20:31.950
They are Zorro's friends.

20:32.000 --> 20:34.950
They help him.

20:35.000 --> 20:37.950
He writes the letter and sends it to the governor.

20:38.000 --> 20:43.950
He smiles and says, I want to see the Pulido family in prison.

20:44.000 --> 20:48.950
I want to see you in prison. Says a man's voice.

20:49.000 --> 20:52.950
Captain Ramon turns around and sees Zorro.

20:53.000 --> 20:54.950
You are a villain.

20:55.000 --> 20:59.950
Fight me, but don't hurt the Pulido family. Says Zorro.

21:00.000 --> 21:02.950
Sergeant Gonzalez, come quickly, says the captain.

21:03.000 --> 21:04.950
Zorro is here.

21:05.000 --> 21:06.950
Zorro disappears.

21:07.000 --> 21:10.950
I am here, Captain. Says Sergeant Gonzalez.

21:11.000 --> 21:13.950
Take all the soldiers and find Zorro.

21:14.000 --> 21:16.950
We must capture him.

21:17.000 --> 21:18.950
The soldiers follow Zorro.

21:19.000 --> 21:20.950
The night is dark.

21:21.000 --> 21:25.950
It is difficult to follow him because his horse is very fast.

21:26.000 --> 21:30.950
The next morning, the soldiers return to the Presidio.

21:31.000 --> 21:33.950
They are tired and angry.

21:34.000 --> 21:36.950
Zorro is still free.

21:37.000 --> 21:40.950
There are many people in front of the Presidio that morning.

21:41.000 --> 21:43.950
Don Diego is there too.

21:44.000 --> 21:46.950
Something is happening.

21:47.000 --> 21:51.950
An old friar is standing before the magistrate.

21:52.000 --> 21:57.950
The old friar is in chains.

21:58.000 --> 22:00.950
I am not a thief. Says the old friar.

22:01.000 --> 22:02.950
I am a poor friar.

22:03.000 --> 22:05.950
What is happening asks Don Diego.

22:06.000 --> 22:07.950
This old friar is a thief.

22:08.000 --> 22:11.950
He must be punished. Answers the magistrate.

22:12.000 --> 22:13.950
That is impossible.

22:14.000 --> 22:15.950
Friar Felipe is an honest man.

22:16.000 --> 22:19.950
I know him. Says Don Diego.

22:20.000 --> 22:23.950
No, you are wrong. Says the cruel magistrate.

22:24.000 --> 22:30.950
He calls two soldiers and says, whip this friar 15 times.

22:31.000 --> 22:33.950
The soldiers whip the old friar.

22:34.000 --> 22:36.950
And he falls to the ground.

22:37.000 --> 22:42.950
Don Diego is very angry because Friar Felipe is his friend.

22:43.000 --> 22:45.950
He returns to his father's hacienda.

22:46.000 --> 22:50.950
Good afternoon, my son. Says his father, Don Alejandro Vega.

22:51.000 --> 22:52.950
I am happy to see you.

22:53.000 --> 22:55.950
Come and tell me about Lolita.

22:56.000 --> 22:57.950
Does she want to marry you?

22:58.000 --> 23:01.950
I like Lolita, but she doesn't like me.

23:02.000 --> 23:03.950
She likes romantic men.

23:04.000 --> 23:06.950
What can I do? Ask Don Diego.

23:07.000 --> 23:09.950
Girls like courageous romantic men.

23:10.000 --> 23:11.950
You must talk about love.

23:12.000 --> 23:14.950
You must play the guitar and sing love songs.

23:15.000 --> 23:16.950
Give her some flowers.

23:17.000 --> 23:18.950
This is what young men do.

23:19.000 --> 23:21.950
Wake up, Diego. Says Don Alejandro.

23:22.000 --> 23:23.950
How ridiculous.

23:24.000 --> 23:27.950
I cannot do these stupid things. Says Don Diego.

23:28.000 --> 23:28.950
You must try.

23:29.000 --> 23:32.950
Lolita is a lovely girl. Says Don Alejandro.

23:33.000 --> 23:34.950
There are many problems in my life.

23:35.000 --> 23:39.000
I want to rest and meditate. Says Don Diego.

23:43.000 --> 23:44.950
Chapter 7.

23:45.000 --> 23:47.950
The Avengers.

23:48.000 --> 23:51.950
In the evening, the magistrate and his friends are in the tavern.

23:52.000 --> 23:55.000
They are laughing about the old friar.

23:56.000 --> 24:00.950
Why are you laughing? Ask some mysterious voice.

24:01.000 --> 24:04.950
They look at the door of the tavern and see Zorro.

24:05.000 --> 24:08.950
He has a pistol in one hand and a sword in the other.

24:09.000 --> 24:13.950
Magistrate, I'm here to punish you. Says Zorro.

24:14.000 --> 24:17.950
Old friar Felipe is not a thief and you know it.

24:18.000 --> 24:21.000
I am an important magistrate.

24:22.000 --> 24:23.950
I am an important magistrate.

24:24.000 --> 24:28.950
I don't like friars because they are your friends, Zorro.

24:29.000 --> 24:33.950
Zorro gives a whip to the magistrate's friend and says...

24:34.000 --> 24:37.950
Now whip this corrupt magistrate 15 times.

24:38.000 --> 24:40.950
But I cannot do this. Says the friend.

24:41.000 --> 24:43.950
Whip him or I whip you. Says Zorro.

24:44.000 --> 24:47.000
The friend whips the magistrate.

24:48.000 --> 24:51.950
After the punishment, the magistrate falls to the ground.

24:52.000 --> 24:56.950
This is how I punish dishonest people. Says Zorro.

24:57.000 --> 25:00.950
The next day, everyone talks about the magistrate's punishment.

25:01.000 --> 25:06.950
A group of young men want to help Captain Ramon arrest Zorro.

25:07.000 --> 25:10.950
They look for him in the hills and in the valleys.

25:11.000 --> 25:14.950
In the evening, they go to the Vega Hacienda.

25:15.000 --> 25:17.950
When Don Alejandro sees them, he says...

25:18.000 --> 25:19.950
Why are you all here?

25:20.000 --> 25:21.950
We are looking for Zorro.

25:22.000 --> 25:24.950
We want to capture the bandit and get the reward.

25:25.000 --> 25:26.950
But now we are tired and hungry.

25:27.000 --> 25:28.950
Can you give us some food?

25:29.000 --> 25:29.950
Yes, of course.

25:30.000 --> 25:30.950
Please come in.

25:31.000 --> 25:35.950
You can put your swords and pistols near the door. Says Don Alejandro.

25:36.000 --> 25:36.950
Sit down.

25:37.000 --> 25:39.950
Eat these cakes and drink this wine.

25:40.000 --> 25:43.950
Don Alejandro and Don Diego talk to the young men.

25:44.000 --> 25:46.950
At 9pm, Don Diego says...

25:47.000 --> 25:48.950
Please excuse me.

25:49.000 --> 25:51.950
I am tired and I am going to bed.

25:52.000 --> 25:52.950
Look, Diego.

25:53.000 --> 25:54.950
These young men are not tired.

25:55.000 --> 25:56.950
It's only 9pm.

25:57.000 --> 26:01.950
You are young, but you are always tired. Says Don Alejandro.

26:02.000 --> 26:03.950
Yes, Father.

26:04.000 --> 26:04.950
You are right.

26:05.000 --> 26:06.950
Good night, everyone.

26:07.000 --> 26:11.000
The others eat, drink, and sing.

26:12.000 --> 26:15.950
At midnight, a masked man appears at the door.

26:16.000 --> 26:20.950
Look, it is Zorro. Says one of the young men.

26:21.000 --> 26:21.950
Zorro the bandit.

26:22.000 --> 26:22.950
Zorro the bandit.

26:23.000 --> 26:24.950
They all say...

26:25.000 --> 26:28.950
Yes, I am Zorro, but I am not a bandit.

26:29.000 --> 26:31.950
I have principles and I fight for them.

26:32.000 --> 26:37.950
In California, we have corrupt political men, cruel magistrates, and dishonest people.

26:38.000 --> 26:39.950
I want to change this.

26:40.000 --> 26:43.950
I fight to help the poor, the natives, and the friars.

26:44.000 --> 26:45.950
What are your principles?

26:46.000 --> 26:47.950
We want to help the poor.

26:48.000 --> 26:51.950
The natives and the friars too. Says one young man.

26:52.000 --> 26:55.950
Our principles are the same. Says another.

26:56.000 --> 26:58.950
Come with me and we can fight together.

26:59.000 --> 27:02.950
We can make California a better place to live. Says Zorro.

27:03.000 --> 27:04.950
But who are you?

27:05.000 --> 27:07.950
Where do you live? Asks a young man.

27:08.000 --> 27:08.950
I can't tell you.

27:09.000 --> 27:10.950
It's a secret. Says Zorro.

27:11.000 --> 27:13.950
The young men talk together.

27:14.000 --> 27:16.950
Yes, we want to fight with you.

27:17.000 --> 27:18.950
We want justice in California.

27:19.000 --> 27:19.950
Our new name is...

27:20.000 --> 27:21.950
The Avengers. Says a young man.

27:22.000 --> 27:23.950
Yes, the Avengers.

27:24.000 --> 27:24.950
The Avengers.

27:25.000 --> 27:25.950
They all say...

27:26.000 --> 27:26.950
Good.

27:27.000 --> 27:29.950
We now fight together. Says Zorro.

27:30.000 --> 27:32.000
And leaves.

27:33.000 --> 27:34.950
California today.

27:35.000 --> 27:39.950
California is an important state of the United States.

27:40.000 --> 27:43.950
About 34 million people live there.

27:44.000 --> 27:48.950
Many old Spanish missions are now important cities and towns.

27:49.000 --> 27:52.950
Many people in California speak Spanish.

27:53.000 --> 27:59.950
Towns, streets, parks, schools, and other places often have Spanish names.

28:00.000 --> 28:04.000
The capital of California is Sacramento.

28:05.000 --> 28:07.950
California is famous for its natural beauty.

28:08.000 --> 28:16.950
There are tall mountains, green valleys, forests, sandy beaches, and hot deserts.

28:17.000 --> 28:30.950
Some beautiful national parks are Yosemite, Sequoia, Kings Canyon, Mirror Woods, Shasta, Death Valley, and Humbled Redwoods.

28:31.000 --> 28:35.950
Young people like Disneyland and the Great America theme park.

28:36.000 --> 28:39.950
Millions of tourists visit California every year.

28:40.000 --> 28:43.950
There are a lot of interesting places to visit.

28:44.000 --> 28:51.950
The University of California, Berkeley and Stanford University are two excellent universities.

28:52.000 --> 28:54.950
California is a cosmopolitan state.

28:55.000 --> 28:59.000
People from all over the world live there.

29:02.000 --> 29:05.950
Chapter 8. The Escape.

29:06.000 --> 29:10.950
The governor of California is here today. Says Sergeant Gonzales.

29:11.000 --> 29:13.950
Good, says Captain Ramon.

29:14.000 --> 29:15.950
I must speak to him.

29:16.000 --> 29:19.950
Good morning, Captain Ramon. Says the governor.

29:20.000 --> 29:21.950
I have your letter.

29:22.000 --> 29:25.950
Thank you for the information about the Pulido family.

29:26.000 --> 29:27.950
They are Zorro's friends.

29:28.000 --> 29:29.950
They are traitors.

29:30.000 --> 29:32.950
We must put them in prison and kill them.

29:33.000 --> 29:34.950
They are dangerous.

29:35.000 --> 29:36.950
What a good idea.

29:37.000 --> 29:41.950
My soldiers can arrest them today, says the captain.

29:42.000 --> 29:47.950
A group of soldiers goes to the Pulido Hacienda.

29:48.000 --> 29:52.950
They arrest Don Carlos, Dona Catalina, and Lolita.

29:53.000 --> 29:54.950
They take them to prison.

29:55.000 --> 29:57.950
Don Carlos is furious.

29:58.000 --> 30:01.000
His wife and daughter cry.

30:04.000 --> 30:07.950
When Don Diego hears about this, he goes to the governor.

30:08.000 --> 30:09.950
He asks him.

30:10.000 --> 30:12.950
Why is the Pulido family in prison?

30:13.000 --> 30:14.950
The governor answers.

30:15.000 --> 30:16.950
They are Zorro's friends.

30:17.000 --> 30:18.950
They help and protect him.

30:19.000 --> 30:20.950
They are traitors.

30:21.000 --> 30:22.950
I cannot believe this.

30:23.000 --> 30:23.950
I know them.

30:24.000 --> 30:25.950
They are honest people.

30:26.000 --> 30:29.950
They don't help bandits. Says Don Diego.

30:30.000 --> 30:31.950
You are wrong, Don Diego.

30:32.000 --> 30:33.950
They must be punished.

30:34.000 --> 30:38.950
The punishment for traitors is death. Says the governor.

30:39.000 --> 30:43.950
Early in the evening, Zorro sends a message to the Avengers.

30:44.000 --> 30:45.950
A message says.

30:46.000 --> 30:48.950
Meet me at midnight at the lake.

30:49.000 --> 30:50.950
Bring your swords and pistols.

30:51.000 --> 30:52.950
Pass the word to everyone.

30:53.000 --> 30:57.950
At midnight, Zorro and the Avengers meet at the lake.

30:58.000 --> 31:00.950
Every Avenger has a mask on his face.

31:01.000 --> 31:02.950
Zorro says.

31:03.000 --> 31:06.950
We are here to rescue Don Pulido and his family.

31:07.000 --> 31:08.950
They must escape from prison.

31:09.000 --> 31:10.950
They are innocent.

31:11.000 --> 31:12.950
We must be silent.

31:13.000 --> 31:14.950
Enter the prison and help them.

31:15.000 --> 31:18.950
Francisco, you take Don Carlos to the village of Pala.

31:19.000 --> 31:22.950
Jose, you take Dona Catalina to the Vega Hacienda.

31:23.000 --> 31:25.950
I want to take Lolita to Friar Felipe.

31:26.000 --> 31:28.950
They must hide for a few days.

31:29.000 --> 31:33.950
Zorro and the Avengers rescue the Pulido family.

31:34.000 --> 31:38.950
Don Carlos and Dona Catalina reach their destination.

31:39.000 --> 31:41.950
The soldiers follow Zorro and Lolita.

31:42.000 --> 31:45.950
Zorro's horse is very fast.

31:46.000 --> 31:50.950
Zorro and Lolita arrive at Friar Felipe's Hacienda.

31:51.000 --> 31:52.950
Zorro says.

31:53.000 --> 31:55.950
Can Lolita stay here with you for a few days?

31:56.000 --> 31:57.950
She is in danger.

31:58.000 --> 32:00.950
Yes, I can protect her. Says Friar Felipe.

32:01.000 --> 32:03.950
Zorro kisses Lolita and says.

32:04.000 --> 32:06.950
Always remember that I love you.

32:07.000 --> 32:10.950
Then he rides away on his horse.

32:11.000 --> 32:14.950
Chapter 9.

32:15.000 --> 32:18.950
The man behind the mask.

32:19.000 --> 32:21.950
The soldiers follow Zorro all night.

32:22.000 --> 32:24.950
They cannot capture him.

32:25.000 --> 32:30.950
The next night, Zorro silently enters the governor's home.

32:31.000 --> 32:34.950
He wants to talk to the governor and Captain Ramon.

32:35.000 --> 32:39.000
They are sitting near the fire.

32:40.000 --> 32:41.950
Zorro enters and says.

32:42.000 --> 32:44.950
Don't move and don't make a noise.

32:45.000 --> 32:46.950
I want to speak to you.

32:47.000 --> 32:50.950
He has a pistol in one hand and a sword in the other.

32:51.000 --> 32:55.950
Zorro, why are you here? Asks the governor.

32:56.000 --> 32:59.950
You are here to die. Says Captain Ramon.

33:00.000 --> 33:01.950
No. Answer Zorro.

33:02.000 --> 33:03.950
I am here to bring justice.

33:04.000 --> 33:05.950
I am here to learn the truth.

33:06.000 --> 33:08.950
Governor, you want to punch the Polito family.

33:09.000 --> 33:09.950
Why?

33:10.000 --> 33:11.950
They are traitors.

33:12.000 --> 33:13.950
They are your friends, Zorro.

33:14.000 --> 33:14.950
They help you.

33:15.000 --> 33:18.950
Your friends are my enemies. Says the governor.

33:19.000 --> 33:19.950
They are not traitors.

33:20.000 --> 33:21.950
They do not help me.

33:22.000 --> 33:23.950
They are not my friends.

33:24.000 --> 33:24.950
He says.

33:25.000 --> 33:26.950
Look at this letter.

33:27.000 --> 33:29.950
It accuses them. Says the governor.

33:30.000 --> 33:32.950
Zorro reads the letter and says.

33:33.000 --> 33:34.950
It is Captain Ramon's letter.

33:35.000 --> 33:36.950
He accuses the Polito family.

33:37.000 --> 33:39.950
Zorro looks at the captain and says.

33:40.000 --> 33:44.950
Captain, you are a liar, but I am here to punish you.

33:45.000 --> 33:47.950
Tell the governor the truth about the Polito family.

33:48.000 --> 33:53.950
Zorro puts his pistol to Captain Ramon's head and says.

33:54.000 --> 33:56.950
Tell the governor the truth or I shoot.

33:57.000 --> 33:59.950
Captain Ramon is silent.

34:00.000 --> 34:01.950
His face is white.

34:02.000 --> 34:04.950
The truth, you liar. Says Zorro.

34:05.000 --> 34:07.950
Yes, I am a liar.

34:08.000 --> 34:10.950
The letter is not true.

34:11.000 --> 34:13.950
This is terrible. Says the governor.

34:14.000 --> 34:15.950
You are a liar.

34:16.000 --> 34:18.950
You cannot be the captain of the Presidio.

34:19.000 --> 34:22.950
At that moment, the captain pulls out his sword.

34:23.000 --> 34:24.950
He begins to fight Zorro.

34:25.000 --> 34:26.950
It is a long sword fight.

34:27.000 --> 34:31.000
In the end, Zorro kills Captain Ramon.

34:32.000 --> 34:35.950
The captain is dead. Says Zorro to the governor.

34:36.000 --> 34:39.950
Outside the governor's home, there are many soldiers.

34:40.000 --> 34:41.950
They want to capture Zorro.

34:42.000 --> 34:44.950
He sees Lolita on her horse.

34:45.000 --> 34:46.950
He shouts.

34:47.000 --> 34:49.950
Lolita, come with me.

34:50.000 --> 34:51.950
We must hide in the old tavern.

34:52.000 --> 34:54.950
This time it is very difficult to escape.

34:55.000 --> 34:56.950
There are soldiers all around us.

34:57.000 --> 34:59.950
I'm happy to be with you, Zorro. Says Lolita.

35:00.000 --> 35:01.950
I'm not scared.

35:02.000 --> 35:05.950
Zorro and Lolita hide inside the old tavern.

35:06.000 --> 35:07.950
The soldiers try to enter.

35:08.000 --> 35:10.950
Zorro is ready to fight.

35:11.000 --> 35:14.950
Suddenly, the Avengers come to rescue Zorro and Lolita.

35:15.000 --> 35:17.950
They explain many things to the governor.

35:18.000 --> 35:20.950
The governor pardons Zorro.

35:21.000 --> 35:23.950
Zorro and Lolita will be ready.

35:24.000 --> 35:24.950
Zorro.

35:25.000 --> 35:28.950
Zorro and Lolita walk out of the old tavern.

35:29.000 --> 35:30.950
They are free.

35:31.000 --> 35:32.950
Everyone is happy and cheers.

35:33.000 --> 35:33.950
Yeah!

35:34.000 --> 35:34.950
Yeah!

35:35.000 --> 35:35.950
Zorro!

35:36.000 --> 35:36.950
Zorro!

35:37.000 --> 35:37.950
The governor says,

35:38.000 --> 35:40.950
Now that you are free, show us your face.

35:41.000 --> 35:41.950
Yes!

35:42.000 --> 35:42.950
Yes!

35:43.000 --> 35:43.950
Yes!

35:44.000 --> 35:44.950
Show us!

35:45.000 --> 35:49.950
The people say, Zorro takes off his black mask.

35:50.000 --> 35:53.950
It's Don Diego Vega! Exclaimed Sergeant Gonzales.

35:54.000 --> 35:56.950
Everyone is very surprised.

35:57.000 --> 36:01.950
My son, Don Diego, I can't believe it! Exclaimed Don Alejandro.

36:02.000 --> 36:04.950
Lolita looks at him and says,

36:05.000 --> 36:05.950
Is this true?

36:06.000 --> 36:07.950
Or is it a dream?

36:08.000 --> 36:09.950
Are you really Don Diego?

36:10.000 --> 36:11.950
Yes, my love.

36:12.000 --> 36:14.950
I am your Don Diego and your Zorro.

36:15.000 --> 36:18.000
He says, Embracing Lolita.
